{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 3 (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`: `validity()`, `impact_plan()`, `pass3_decide`, `pass3_over_findings`, `DEFAULT_BLOCK_THRESHOLD`, per-criterion `block_threshold`/`default_posture` in `criteria_routing.json`) is deterministic and every input it needs — the Pass-2 `verification` vector, `block_threshold`, `blocking_enabled`, `review_phase` — is in the v2 sidecar. `docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` and `docs/experiments/calibrate_plan_review_thresholds.py` prove the replay works but are one-off scripts with hardcoded baselines. Any proposal touching Pass-3 logic or thresholds should be assessable over the corpus for free.\n\n`review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, *, threshold_for, impact_fn=None, execution_review=False)` is the OVERLAY-CAPABLE kernel entrypoint: `threshold_for` is a caller-supplied `Callable[[Sequence[str]], tuple[float, bool]]` resolving a candidate's per-criterion thresholds/postures, and `impact_fn` is a caller-supplied candidate impact model. `orchestrator.pass3_over_findings` is NOT this — it is a thin wrapper that hardcodes `impact_fn=impact_plan` and resolves thresholds only from the LIVE plan-review registry via a private `_threshold_for`; it cannot take a candidate overlay. Baseline replay calls the kernel function with `impact_fn=impact_plan` (matching current production) and a `threshold_for` built from the LIVE `criteria_routing.json`; a candidate replay calls it with an overlay JSON's thresholds/postures and/or a substitute `impact_fn`.\n\n`docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` already solves the plan-v4→plan-v5 cross-version replay problem: pre-v5 sidecars carry ORDINAL grades (`low|medium|high`) on axes like `undecomposed`/`dod_uncertifiable` that plan-v5's `impact_plan` kind model rejects directly. That script's `classify(axis, text)` (regex `RULES`, gap-biased: a genuine-gap body maps to a FLOORING kind, a specificity/framing complaint maps to advisory) maps each graded row's finding body to its nearest plan-v5 KIND, and `rescore(attrs, kinds)` then feeds the mapped kinds through `decide._PLAN_GRADE_MAPS` to get a plan-v5-comparable score. Tier-0's plan-v4→v5 replay reuses this SAME mapping (`classify`/`RULES`), not a fictional direct feed of old ordinal grades into `impact_plan`.\n\nTicket-level labels (`labels.py`, expectable-clownlike-ynambu, closed) require a `show_ticket` call per ticket, confirmed too slow at full-corpus (~6400-ticket) scale — the committed evidence there is a real 40-ticket subset, not the full corpus. Tier-0's own Pass-3 replay needs NONE of that: every input (`verification`, `criteria`, `block_threshold`, `blocking_enabled`) already lives in the corpus's recovered `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar `data`, with no ticket-level enrichment. Label-proxy metrics are therefore SEPARATE, OPTIONAL, best-effort: computed only over whatever committed `labels-<hash>.jsonl` the caller supplies (real coverage, not assumed complete), with the report stating that coverage fraction.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (+ `report.py`, `__main__.py`):\n\n- Input: the corpus (via `corpus.build_corpus`), an OPTIONAL `labels_path` (a `labels-<hash>.jsonl` read via `labels.load_labels`; absent/mismatched-hash means label-proxy metrics are omitted, never a hard failure), and a **candidate** = a Python callable/module path for `impact_fn`, a routing-overlay JSON (thresholds/postures) building a `threshold_for` callable, and `[verify]` config overrides. Default candidate = current live `criteria_routing.json` + `impact_plan` (the identity check).\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py`: `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate <name>` subcommand dispatch (the package's module entry point; `ledger.print_summary()` is wired in here too per the ledger ticket's own note) — argparse over `tier0`/future subcommands, resolving `--candidate` to the corpus/labels/overlay inputs above and calling `tier0.run(...)`.\n- Run `review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings(findings, verifs, threshold_for=..., impact_fn=...)` for baseline and candidate over every corpus review's surfaced findings (`sidecar.surfaced_findings`); keep the stored decision (from the sidecar `data`) as the historical reference too. Pure computation over already-recovered sidecar data — no `show_ticket` — so this is the part the 5-minute timing AC applies to.\n- Plan-v4→v5 replay (AC2): for pre-v5 sidecars, apply `plan_v5_rescore.classify`/`RULES` to map each graded axis to its plan-v5 kind BEFORE feeding `impact_plan`, reusing that script's mapping rather than reimplementing it (import it, or port its `RULES`/`classify` verbatim if the script isn't itself importable as a package module — confirm which at implementation time).\n- Report (`tier0-<candidate-name>-<date>.md` + JSON): verdict flip matrix (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE), friction rate, per-criterion block/advisory/drop deltas, priority distribution shift. IF `labels_path` supplied: label-proxy metrics (block rate on `escaped_defect`/`completion_failed_after_pass` vs `clean_close` tickets, `resolved_by_author` share) computed ONLY over reviews whose ticket has a label row, with the report stating that coverage fraction and annotating deltas against the labels ticket's noise band. ELSE the report states label-proxy metrics were not computed.\n- Post-verdict floors (novelty/completion/drift) replayed only when their inputs are present in the sidecar; otherwise reported as not replayed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier0.py` (new) — Pass-3 replay\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/report.py` (new) — diff report rendering\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (new) — `python -m ...` module entry point / subcommand dispatch\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier0-*.md` (generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier0.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: identity replay of a fixture corpus (using `review_kernel.decide.pass3_over_findings` with `threshold_for`/`impact_fn` matching the fixture's stored decision) yields zero diffs; a candidate overlay lowering one criterion's threshold flips exactly the fixture findings whose priority sits between old and new thresholds; a v1 sidecar lacking `block_threshold` is skipped and counted; a pre-v5 graded row is classified to a plan-v5 kind via the reused mapping before rescoring; label-proxy metrics are omitted (not crashed) when no `labels_path` is supplied, and computed with an explicit coverage fraction when one is; `__main__.py`'s `tier0` subcommand dispatches to `tier0.run(...)` with parsed args.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current` over the real corpus reports zero verdict flips against stored decisions for reviews whose `impact_model_version` matches current; checked by the generated report.\n- [ ] Replaying the plan-v4→plan-v5 change (via the reused `plan_v5_rescore` grade→kind mapping) reproduces its documented direction and approximate magnitude; checked against `docs/calibration/`.\n- [ ] The report contains verdict flip matrix, friction rate, and per-criterion deltas from the pure Pass-3 replay; checked by inspection of one report.\n- [ ] IF a labels file is supplied, the report additionally contains label-proxy recall/false-positive metrics with their coverage fraction, annotated relative to the noise band; checked by inspection when a labels file is available.\n- [ ] The Pass-3 replay itself (excluding any optional label-proxy step) completes in under 5 minutes on a laptop over the real corpus, with zero LLM calls; checked by timing and by running without provider credentials.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788083700420421389,"uuid":"2501382b-0689-4e18-bcc9-34036a53ab1a"}